A||N||8||Butter||Door handle getting hard to open||||1||
Z||000000||Butter||07-17-2001||04:09 PM||||Folks,<BR>I live around dusty gravel roads and my right outside door handle is too hard to open.  The right side is also getting harder.  Is there a particular place to lube this and what lubrication should I use?||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT-maniac||07-17-2001||08:58 PM||||You'll have to pull the inside door panel off to access the parts. The door handle pushes down on a rod which in turn pushes down a spring loaded lever which operates the lock mechanism. With the door panel off you can easily see this mechanism. Try lifting the handle a few times to see how it operates and check to see if the rod is binding on anything. There's a kind of metal hook that comes out of the door and the rod is supposed to be behind this. And the rod is supposed to be bent. Then I would clean off the whole mechanism with some WD 40 and lube it up with some white lithium grease.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||07-18-2001||09:44 AM||||GT-maniac,<BR>Thanks, and one other question.  How much harder is it to replace the door lock as it is having trouble also?<p>[This message has been edited by Butter (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||k2m4||07-18-2001||10:17 AM||||Its not hard its just a pain in the ass. When i replaced my locks i took both the inner and outer panels off. it was reletively easy but just time consuming!<BR>k||||reg||1
Z||000004||Butter||07-18-2001||10:49 AM||||Thanks Yall,<BR>I be workin' on this sometime soon.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||Johnson's85SE||07-18-2001||12:48 PM||||Hey GT-Maniac, How old are you and what is your name? I used to live in Grande Prairie. Names Chris Johnson. <P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT-maniac||07-18-2001||02:55 PM|||| [QUOTE]Originally posted by Butter:<BR>[b]GT-maniac,<BR>Thanks, and one other question.  How much harder is it to replace the door lock as it is having trouble also?<P>As K2m4 says it's really not hard to do if you have the outer door skin off. Having struggled with trying do it from the inside I can safely say taking the skin off is 100 times easier. And the skins are easy to take off too. Just follow the directions in Ogre's cave. I bought my new locks from the dealer and had them keyed to my key there.<P><p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||1
